    "id": "d1",
    "name": "ASP4345 or AF710B",
    "function": "D1-responsive hold versus M1 and sigma-1 coupling.",
    "mechanism": "D1 potentiation depends on endogenous dopamine and the circuit\u2019s arousal state; too much D1 signaling can weaken a representation that benefits at a lower level. AF710B connects muscarinic and sigma-1 signaling through a different architecture. These are state-dependent alternatives, not two ways of increasing a single universal working-memory variable.",
