    "name": "Senicapoc or ibudilast or dapansutrile",
    "function": "Glial ion-channel signaling, broader inflammatory modulation or NLRP3.",
    "mechanism": "Senicapoc targets KCa3.1; dapansutrile addresses the NLRP3 inflammasome; ibudilast acts more broadly. Pairing a glial branch with MAO-B modulation only makes causal sense when the inflammatory and metabolic processes are jointly active. These compounds are not equivalent ways of removing an undifferentiated \u201cfog.\u201d",
