        "name": "Creatine monohydrate; guanidinoacetic acid (GAA) + betaine as the methylation-coupled extension",
        "function": "Phosphagen buffering across repeated demand.",
        "mechanism": "Creatine buffers ATP through phosphocreatine; it does not create net energy. GAA adds a precursor route whose conversion consumes methyl groups, linking the energy objective to betaine-dependent methyl balance. Cyclocreatine is a distinct phosphagen branch, not an interchangeable creatine quantity. The relevant endpoint is recovery between demands, not merely a larger precursor pool.",
